    </note>
  </subsection>
  <subsection title="Multiply Monomials">
    <p>Since a monomial is an algebraic expression, we can use the properties for simplifying expressions with exponents to multiply the monomials.</p>
    <example number="10.26">
      <problem>
        <p>Multiply: $${{({4x^{2}})}{({- 5x^{3}})}}.$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table summary="Steps to multiply two monomials, illustrating the rearrangement of factors using the Commutative Property to simplify the expression.">
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell>$$({4x^{2}}){( - 5x^{3}})$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Use the Commutative Property to rearrange the factors.</cell>
              <cell>$$4 \cdot {(-5)} \cdot x^{2} \cdot x^{3}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Multiply.</cell>
              <cell>$$- 20x^{5}$$</cell>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </solution>
    </example>
    <note type="Try It" number="10.51">
      <p>Multiply: $${{({7x^{7}})}{({- 8x^{4}})}}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <note type="Try It" number="10.52">
      <p>Multiply: $${{({- 9y^{4}})}{({- 6y^{5}})}}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <example number="10.27">
      <problem>
        <p>Multiply: $${\left( {\frac{3}{4}\mspace{2mu} c^{3}d} \right){({12cd^{2}})}}.$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table summary="Step-by-step simplification of an algebraic expression, showing the application of the Commutative Property to rearrange factors before multiplication.">
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell>$$\left( \frac{3}{4}\mspace{2mu} c^{3}d \right)(12cd^{2})$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Use the Commutative Property to rearrange the factors.</cell>
              <cell>$$\frac{3}{4} \cdot 12 \cdot c^{3} \cdot c \cdot d \cdot d^{2}$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Multiply.</cell>
              <cell>$$9c^{4}d^{3}$$</cell>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </solution>
    </example>
    <note type="Try It" number="10.53">
      <p>Multiply: $${\left( {\frac{4}{5}\mspace{2mu} m^{4}n^{3}} \right){({15mn^{3}})}}.$$</p>
    </note>
    <note type="Try It" number="10.54">
